                <h2>Case Opening: A Tool App's Cold Launch Dilemma</h2>
<p>A tool app team entered TikTok Shop in Q4 2024, targeting 500K GMV in the first month. They had two media buyers, one creative designer, and a budget of $20,000. However, they hit a wall within the first week of launch.</p>
<p><strong>Problem Diagnosis:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Severe creative shortage: only 8 videos produced in the first week</li>
<li>Neither organic nor paid traffic drove conversions</li>
<li>CTR at just 0.8%, far below the category average of 2.5%</li>
<li>Account struggled to scale; single ad sets exhausted budgets under $50/day</li>
</ul>
<p>This wasn't a capability issue — it was a timing problem in building the creative pool. During the cold launch phase, TikTok's algorithm is in its learning period, and creatives are the "fuel." Without enough fuel, or with low-quality fuel, the account won't run.</p>
<h2>Diagnosis: Three Core Metrics for Cold Launch Creative Pools</h2>
<p>Before diving into optimization, the team established clear benchmarks. During cold launch, creative pool health depends on three metrics:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Metric</th>
<th>Healthy Value</th>
<th>Danger Zone</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Creative Volume</td>
<td>≥30/week</td>
<td>&lt;15/week</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>CTR</td>
<td>≥2%</td>
<td>&lt;1%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Creative Survival Rate</td>
<td>≥20% past learning phase</td>
<td>&lt;10%</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>This team's creative volume and CTR both triggered warnings, indicating problems on both the supply side and creative quality side.</p>
<h2>Action Plan: Four Steps to Build a Cold Launch Creative Pool</h2>
<h3>Step 1: Deconstruct Product Selling Points into 5-8 Creative Angles</h3>
<p>Don't start by pursuing "cinematic quality." Cold launch requires rapid iteration. The team mapped the app's core use cases into these angles:</p>
<ul>
<li>Pain point resonance: User daily pain + product solution</li>
<li>Results showcase: Before/After comparison</li>
<li>Tutorial style: Complete a task in 3 steps</li>
<li>Trending angle: Tie into current TikTok memes</li>
<li>UGC style: Simulate real user testimonials</li>
</ul>
<h3>Step 2: Mass-Produce MVP Creatives</h3>
<p>At least 4 videos per angle, keeping each to 15-30 seconds. Key principles:</p>
<ul>
<li>Hook in the first 3 seconds (suspense, numbers, conflict)</li>
<li>Large subtitles, clear audio</li>
<li>Use trending TikTok background music</li>
<li>Direct CTAs — no beating around the bush</li>
</ul>
<h3>Step 3: Tiered Testing — Don't Put All Eggs in One Basket</h3>
<p>On day one of creative rollout, the team implemented tiered testing:</p>
<ul>
<li>60% budget: New creative A/B testing ($200-300/day per creative)</li>
<li>30% budget: Extend top two performers from the previous week</li>
<li>10% budget: Explore new angles (low-cost testing)</li>
</ul>
<h3>Step 4: 48-Hour Rapid Iteration</h3>
<p>No time for slow optimization during cold launch. Protocol: any creative with CTR below 1% after 48 hours gets paused immediately and replaced with a new angle; creatives exceeding 2.5% CTR get budget increases for further testing.</p>
<h2>Results: From Collapse to Stable Scaling</h2>
<p>After three weeks of adjustment, the tool app team's creative pool showed significant improvement:</p>
<ul>
<li>Creative inventory: grew from 8 to a stable 35+ per week</li>
<li>CTR: improved from 0.8% to 2.2%</li>
<li>Peak daily spend per creative: broke through from $50 to $800</li>
<li>First-month GMV actual: approximately 480K, slightly below target, but the account entered a positive loop</li>
</ul>
<p>Only 5-6 creatives truly performed, but these core creatives supported stable spending going forward.</p>
<h2>Three Key Principles of the Cold Launch Creative SOP</h2>
<p>Reflecting on this case, three principles are worth remembering for all TikTok Shop newcomers:</p>
<ol>
<li>
<p><strong>Volume is the foundation</strong>: Without enough creatives, you can't test; without testing, you have no data; without data, you can't optimize. Aim for at least 30 creatives in the first week.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Direction matters more than quality</strong>: Rather than spending a week crafting one "perfect" creative, produce 10 MVP creatives across different angles quickly. Once the right direction is found, quality improvements follow naturally.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Iteration speed determines account fate</strong>: TikTok's algorithm learning phase is only 7 days. Creatives that don't show positive data within 7 days can essentially be abandoned. Save budgets for the winning creatives discovered through rapid testing.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p>Cold launch isn't mysticism — it's a methodology-driven creative war.</p>
